1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:05,943
Hy Image 3.5 renders type beautifully, but small print slips.

2
00:00:05,943 --> 00:00:12,570
On this copper test render, a world total of 23,000 came out as 28,000.

3
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:15,988
Summaries, spelled Summaties.

4
00:00:15,988 --> 00:00:18,560
Four times, on two topics.

5
00:00:19,110 --> 00:00:21,962
And tick numbers nobody asked for.

6
00:00:21,962 --> 00:00:24,310
One Hy edit fixed all three.

7
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:32,220
Across 13 runs for this set, Plate flagged 8 misspellings and removed text that Hy invented.

8
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:34,081
Here's the loop.

9
00:00:34,081 --> 00:00:37,770
Paste a brief, and pick a format and a style.

10
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:42,770
Meta's Muse Spark 1.3 writes a spec with every string locked.

11
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,920
Hy Image renders it.

12
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:50,760
Muse Spark, blind to the spec, reads it back, and code diffs every label.

13
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:55,790
On this run, Hy pointed a note about the whole chart at Zambia.

14
00:00:56,340 --> 00:01:00,928
Plate flagged it, and one Hy edit erased just that line.

15
00:01:00,928 --> 00:01:06,500
Fixes are reference edits or corrected re-renders, up to six passes.

16
00:01:07,050 --> 00:01:13,610
Checked 31 of 31, with takeaways, a caption, alt text and the data table.

17
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,408
It isn't perfect.

18
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,903
It missed quarters drawn with a g.

19
00:01:17,903 --> 00:01:23,040
A human caught it, and one Hy edit changed that line and nothing else.

20
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:25,941
The result: Material Facts.

21
00:01:25,941 --> 00:01:32,470
Copper: Chile mined more than the United States, China and Russia combined.

22
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:37,820
Coffee: Brazil grows more than the next four countries together.

23
00:01:38,370 --> 00:01:43,330
Cotton: China grew more than Brazil and the United States combined.

24
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:51,400
Lithium: Australia, China and Chile mined nearly three-quarters of world output, not counting the U.S.

25
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:52,575
Plate.

26
00:01:52,575 --> 00:01:56,739
Every infographic pixel by Hy Image 3.5.

27
00:01:56,739 --> 00:01:59,550
The code is open on GitHub.
